.env
.env.local
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
dist/
.replit
replit.nix
*.tsbuildinfo

# Cloudflare local dev state and secrets, never committed.
#
# The shop-worker/ rules below were written when wrangler was only ever run
# from inside that directory. Running it from the repository root — which is
# what a `wrangler deploy --config shop-worker/wrangler.toml` invocation does —
# creates a SECOND cache at the root that no rule covered, so it showed up as
# untracked on a clean tree. Both locations are now ignored.
.wrangler/
shop-worker/.wrangler/
.dev.vars
shop-worker/.dev.vars

# Owner Admin deployment packages.
#
# dist/ above already covers the packages this repo builds itself. This covers
# the ones a person ends up with beside the admin source: a bundle downloaded
# from Cloudflare and re-zipped by the browser lands here as `*.zip.zip`. A
# built admin package carries whatever configuration it was built with, and
# this repository is public, so it must never be committed by accident.
#
# Scoped to admin/ deliberately. A blanket `*.zip` would also mask the
# deployment package the Shop Admin branch commits under dist/, and that is a
# separate piece of work whose choices this rule has no business overriding.
admin/*.zip
